        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1863">

                <pb facs="1373" n="1257" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 419.11H23/42.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 514.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my despatch No. 510 of May
                    15 in the case of William T. Harrington, I have the honor to enclose a copy of
                    the Spanish text of the reply from the Panaman Foreign Office, a translation of
                    which was sent with the despatch above mentioned.</p>
                <p>Unless in the meantime the Department may desire to instruct me specially with
                    reference to the proper response to this note, I shall attempt to answer the
                    arguments presented and assert claim for a definite indemnity in the sum of
                    $5,000.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Jennings Price.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
